<h1>gamepad_get_device_count</h1>
<p>This function either gives you the number of game pads connected, <i>or</i> the number of available &quot;slots&quot; for game pads to be connected to.</p>
<p>The actual return value will depend on the platform and the internal configuration of that platform and as such this function can be used in conjunction with the function <a href="gamepad_is_connected.htm"><span class="inline">gamepad_is_connected()</span></a> to make sure of the exact number of pads connected at any time.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">gamepad_get_device_count();</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">var gp_num = gamepad_get_device_count();<br/>
for (var i = 0; i &lt; gp_num; i++;)<br/>
{<br/>
    if (gamepad_is_connected(i))<br/>
    {<br/>
        global.gp[i] = true;<br/>
    }<br/>
    else<br/>
    {<br/>
        global.gp[i] = false;<br/>
    }<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code loops through the available game pads (or gamepad slots) and then checks each one for a connected gamepad. The returned value is then used to set a global array to <span class="inline">true</span> or <span class="inline">false</span> for use in future checks.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
